BEGIN CRUMB
v=1.2
kind=task
title=Add per-token rate limiting to the public API
source=session.capture
project=api-gateway
---
[goal]
Per-token rate limiting so one client cannot starve the shared worker pool.
Limit on the token, not the client IP — everything is behind a shared LB.

[context]
Register the limiter in apply_middleware() in src/gateway/server.py; implement
it in src/gateway/middleware.py matching the existing
`async __call__(self, scope, receive, send)` shape. src/gateway/auth.py
populates scope["state"]["token_id"], so the limiter must be registered after
auth or every request looks anonymous. Counters go in the Redis already at
config/redis.yaml. Reproduced on main@a1b2c3d: one client at 200 rps takes
other tokens' p95 from 180ms to 4.2s.

[constraints]
- No breaking changes to the existing response schema
- No third-party dependencies beyond redis-py
- Sliding window, not fixed — a fixed window allows a 2x burst across the
  boundary, which starves the pool again

[handoff]
- to=any do=implement the sliding-window limiter in src/gateway/middleware.py
- to=any do=create config/limits.yaml and read per-token defaults from it
- to=any do=add tests/test_rate_limit.py, verified by `pytest tests/test_rate_limit.py -q`
- [x] reproduced the starvation with tools.loadgen on main@a1b2c3d
END CRUMB
